# voice packs are large and fetched separately
#
# The .voice blobs are concatenated sample audio: pinyin.voice is 122 MB for
# the 44.1 kHz Mandarin pack, jyutping.voice 5.5 MB. The .index files are small
# (tens of KB) and stay tracked, because they describe the offsets into the blob
# and are what a reader needs in order to interpret it.
/ekho-data/*.voice
/ekho-data/pinyin/
/ekho-data/jyutping/
/ekho-data/alphabet/
/ekho-data/piper/

# Converted-pack backups: ekho-data/pinyin.* are the 48 kHz pack
# (scripts/convert-voice.c); the upstream 44.1 kHz originals stay next to them
# as *.44k -- scripts/reg-44k.sh renders the byte-exact regression reference
# with them -- and the rejected 8 kHz experiment as *.8k.
/ekho-data/*.voice.*
/ekho-data/*.index.*

# scratch
*.wav.tmp
/_work/